issue.body:
The implementation of fault injection includes several items:
1. Interpret xDS configs and craft service config;
1. Parse service config for fault injection policy;
1. Apply fault injection policy to CallData;
1. Iterate through headers for overriding setting if any;
1. Enforce active faults count;
1. Inject RPC delay;
1. Inject RPC abort;
1. ~~Inject response rate limit.~~

This PR is the first batch that implements 2, 3, 4, 5, 7. I hope to get early feedback, so if I got something very wrong I will have the time to pivot.

---

For item 1, I can go ahead to implement it in the `XdsConfigSelector` if it won't conflict with Donna's work.

For item 6 (RPC delay), is `StartTransportStreamOpBatch` a valid place to hook an extra layer of callback to inject the fixed delay?

For item 8 (response rate limit), I might delay it because now I don't have an elegant solution to throttle the responses.

---

**Update**, this PR implements all items above. It should be sufficient for Core to be ready for upcoming interop tests. 

